    {
      "id": "p04",
      "art": "assets/gandhi_s_indigo_truth/img/p04.png",
      "shot": "bird’s-eye wide of Champaran countryside showing scattered villages, indigo patches, and a distant planter factory chimney",
      "mood": "battle",
      "lines": [
        {
          "type": "narration",
          "role": "narrator",
          "text": {
            "en": "Champaran was not a battlefield, but a patchwork of estates where tenants, tied by tinkathia, had to grow indigo on fixed land even when the blue dye had lost its shine on world markets.",
            "hi": "चंपारण कोई मैदान-ए-जंग नहीं, बल्कि जमींदारियों की जाल थी, जहाँ किरायेदार टिंकठिया से बंधे, तय जमीन पर नील उगाने को मजबूर थे, जबकि नीला रंग दुनिया में अपनी चमक खो चुका था।"
          },
